iod_end": "2024-01-28", "section": "mdna", "score": 1.1754, "filing_name": "NVIDIA Corporation 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581024000029/nvda-20240128.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "NVDA_10K_2024-01-28__mdna__0017", "ticker": "NVDA", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2024", "period_end": "2024-01-28", "section": "mdna", "score": 1.1233, "filing_name": "NVIDIA Corporation 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581024000029/nvda-20240128.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "NVDA_10K_2024-01-28__mdna__0022", "ticker": "NVDA", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2024", "period_end": "2024-01-28", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.9662, "filing_name": "NVIDIA Corporation 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581024000029/nvda-20240128.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "NVDA_10K_2024-01-28__financial_statements__0119", "ticker": "NVDA", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2024", "period_end": "2024-01-28", "section": "financial_statements", "score": 1.1433, "filing_name": "NVIDIA Corporation 10-K FY2024", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1045810/000104581024000029/nvda-20240128.htm", "truncated": false}], "collapsed_near_duplicates": 131, "dropped_candidates": 855, "token_estimate": 30557, "gaps": [], "degraded": []}, "answer": {"direct_answer": "NVIDIA's revenue rose from $60,922 million in fiscal 2024 (ended January 28, 2024) to $130,497 million in fiscal 2025 (ended January 26, 2025) [facts:NVDA:Revenues:FY2025], and quarterly revenue reached $57,006 million in Q3 fiscal 2026 (ended October 26, 2025), up 62% from a year ago [facts:NVDA:Revenues:Q3FY2026]. Fiscal 2025 revenue growth of 114% over fiscal 2024 compares with 126% growth in fiscal 2024 over the prior fiscal year [NVDA_10K_2025-01-26__mdna__0016] [NVDA_10K_2024-01-28__mdna__0006]. Year-over-year quarterly growth peaked at 262% in Q1 fiscal 2025 (ended April 28, 2024) and has since moderated to 69% in Q1 fiscal 2026, 56% in Q2 fiscal 2026, and 62% in Q3 fiscal 2026 [NVDA_10Q_2024-04-28__mdna__0007] [NVDA_10Q_2025-10-26__mdna__0006]. The growth driver shifted from the Hopper platform to Blackwell, which the Q3 fiscal 2026 filing says is the majority of Data Center revenue [NVDA_10K_2025-01-26__mdna__0000] [NVDA_10Q_2025-10-26__mdna__0002]. The filings flag outlook risks: H20 export licensing requirements that management says will negatively affect future revenue, and customers' availability of data centers, energy, and capital [NVDA_10Q_2025-04-27__mdna__0002] [NVDA_10Q_2025-10-26__mdna__0002]. The filings give no numeric revenue guidance.", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "NVDA", "company": "NVIDIA Corporation", "findings": [{"point": "Annual revenue went from $60,922 million in fiscal 2024 (ended January 28, 2024), up 126% from $26,974 million, to $130,497 million in fiscal 2025 (ended January 26, 2025), up 114%.", "citations": ["NVDA_10K_2024-01-28__mdna__0006", "NVDA_10K_2025-01-26__mdna__0016"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Year-over-year quarterly revenue growth was 262% in Q1 fiscal 2025 (ended April 28, 2024), 122% in Q2 fiscal 2025 (ended July 28, 2024), and 94% in Q3 fiscal 2025 (ended October 27, 2024).", "citations": ["NVDA_10Q_2024-04-28__mdna__0007", "NVDA_10Q_2024-07-28__mdna__0007", "NVDA_10Q_2024-10-27__mdna__0008"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Fiscal 2026 quarters show year-over-year growth of 69% in Q1 (ended April 27, 2025), 56% in Q2 (ended July 27, 2025), and 62% in Q3 (ended October 26, 2025), with Q3 revenue of $57,006 million.", "citations": ["NVDA_10Q_2025-04-27__mdna__0006", "NVDA_10Q_2025-07-27__mdna__0006", "NVDA_10Q_2025-10-26__mdna__0006"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Q3 fiscal 2026 Data Center revenue was $51.2 billion, up 66% from a year ago, driven by accelerated computing, powerful AI models, and agentic applications, with Blackwell the majority of Data Center revenue.", "citations": ["NVDA_10Q_2025-10-26__mdna__0007", "NVDA_10Q_2025-10-26__mdna__0002"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Outlook-related risks: the H20 export licensing requirement (with a $4.5 billion charge in Q1 fiscal 2026) will negatively affect future revenue, and shortages of customer data center, energy, or capital resources could impact future revenue.", "citations": ["NVDA_10Q_2025-04-27__mdna__0002", "NVDA_10Q_2025-10-26__mdna__0002"], "unverified": false}]}], "comparison_table": {"columns": ["Period (fiscal label, end date)", "Revenue ($ millions)", "Year-over-year growth"], "rows": [["Fiscal 2024, ended January 28, 2024 [NVDA_10K_2024-01-28__mdna__0006]", "$60,922 million", "126%"], ["Fiscal 2025, ended January 26, 2025 [NVDA_10K_2025-01-26__mdna__0016]", "$130,497 million", "114%"], ["Q1 fiscal 2025, ended April 28, 2024 [NVDA_10Q_2024-04-28__mdna__0007]", "$26,044 million", "262%"], ["Q1 fiscal 2026, ended April 27, 2025 [NVDA_10Q_2025-04-27__mdna__0006]", "$44,062 million", "69%"], ["Q3 fiscal 2026, ended October 26, 2025 [NVDA_10Q_2025-10-26__mdna__0006]", "$57,006 million", "62%"]]}, "citations": [{"chunk_id": "NVDA_10K_2024-01-28__mdna__0006", "claim": "Fiscal 2024 revenue and growth", "quote": "Revenue | $ 60,922 | $ 26,974 | Up 126%"}, {"chunk_id": "NVDA_10K_2025-01-26__mdna__0016", "claim": "Fiscal 2025 revenue growth 114%", "quote": "Total | $ 130,497 | $ 60,922 | $ 69,575 | 114 | %"}, {"chunk_id": "facts:NVDA:Revenues:FY2025", "claim": "Fiscal 2025 revenue value", "quote": "130,497 | USD millions | FY2025 | period end 2025-01-26"}, {"chunk_id": "facts:NVDA:Revenues:Q3FY2026", "claim": "Q3 fiscal 2026 revenue value", "quote": "57,006 | USD millions | Q3 FY2026 | period end 2025-10-26"}, {"chunk_id": "NVDA_10Q_2024-04-28__mdna__0007", "claim": "Q1 fiscal 2025 growth 262%", "quote": "Revenue | $ 26,044 | $ 22,103 | $ 7,192 | 18 | % | 262 | %"}, {"chunk_id": "NVDA_10Q_2024-07-28__mdna__0007", "claim": "Q2 fiscal 2025 growth 122%", "quot